=== COLUMNS (0-indexed j = col-1) vs power sums Sum_{k=1}^{m} k^j ===
  col j=0: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
    Sum k^0: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]   MATCH=False  <-- DEVIATES (Moser-type)
  col j=1: [1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21]
    Sum k^1: [1, 3, 6, 10, 15]   MATCH=False  <-- DEVIATES (Moser-type)
  col j=2: [1, 5, 14, 30, 55]
    Sum k^2: [1, 5, 14, 30]   MATCH=False  <-- DEVIATES (Moser-type)
  col j=3: [1, 9, 37, 101]
    Sum k^3: [1, 9, 36]   MATCH=False  <-- DEVIATES (Moser-type)
  col j=4: [1, 17, 99]
    Sum k^4: [1, 17]   MATCH=False  <-- DEVIATES (Moser-type)
  col j=5: [1, 33]
    Sum k^5: [1]   MATCH=False  <-- DEVIATES (Moser-type)

=== SUBDIAGONAL (col=row-1) and last diagonal ===
  subdiagonal T(r,r-1): [2, 3, 5, 9, 17, 33]   vs 2^x+1: [3, 5, 9, 17, 33, 65]
  main diagonal T(r,r): [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1] (all 1)

